body:
**Shape.** `using var a := …; a.Dispose(); Take(move a);` — the scope pin's move-out prohibition is skipped once the binding is explicitly disposed.

```bezel
module Probe;

public sealed class Q
  private _id: int;
  public constructor(id: int)
    _id := id;
  end constructor;
  destructor
    Console.WriteLine($"D:{_id}");
  end destructor;
  public method Use()
    Console.WriteLine($"U:{_id}");
  end Use;
end Q;

public sealed class R
  private _id: int;
  public owned f: Q;
  public constructor(id: int, owned q: Q)
    _id := id;
    f := q;
  end constructor;
  destructor
    Console.WriteLine($"D:{_id}");
  end destructor;
  public method Use()
    Console.WriteLine($"U:{_id}");
  end Use;
  public static method Take(owned r: R)
    using var k := move r;
  end Take;
  public static method Body()
    using var a := new R(2, new Q(1));
    a.Dispose();                      // site-announced kill (admitted, §28.10)
    R.Take(move a);                   // move OUT of a using var: A5 says compile error; accepted with the §28.2 warning
  end Body;
end R;

public class Program
  public static method Main(): int
    R.Body();
    Console.WriteLine("END");
    return 0;
  end Main;
end Program;
```

**Measured on r35.** Both modes: compiles with the §28.2 warning only (`move from a local \`a\` already disposed at this point`); runs `D:2 D:1 END`, exit 0. Without the `Dispose()` line the same `Take(move a)` is correctly rejected (`cannot move out of \`using var\` \`a\`; \`using var\` is scope-bound (§28.3)`). Siblings: `using var a; a.Dispose(); var b := move a;`, `… using var b := move a;`.

**Spec (v0.345).** §28.3.7: *"A `using var` is owned but is additionally bound to its scope: it cannot be moved out of, only borrowed from (axiom A5)."* §28.10: *"`using var` is a scope pin (axiom A5): it is implicitly non-reassignable"*. A5 is a property of the binding, not of its state; §28.2's warning regime covers the *use* of an explicitly-disposed binding and does not lift the pin. Expected: the A5 compile error (the warning is secondary).

**Differential numbers.** 17 of 3,000 sampled programs in the `pins` fragment (vars 3 / len 4) and 22 of 3,000 in the try/while sample: every model `A5-move-out-of-using-var` rejection whose move follows a `Dispose()` is accepted by r35.

**Measured on r35** (`bezelc 0.0.0-f6863e62`, the 2026-10-27 release build; main may have moved since). Found by the model-vs-compiler differential (`scratch/bzdiff`, proposal 0047 §5.3 / soundness README §3.2): the executable ownership model (bzcore L1, spec v0.345) and `bezelc` disagree on this program; the model's verdict is the spec's sentence quoted above.
